  "goodToKnow": "Der Rebell (die Rebellin) is a rebel, in war or in life: Er war schon immer ein Rebell. It's a weak noun, so it adds -en in all cases except the nominative singular: den Rebellen, dem Rebellen. Rebellisch means rebellious, and rebellieren to rebel. In German history, der Bauernkrieg (1524–25) was a large peasants' rebellion. Stress is on the last syllable: re-BELL."
